Choose Your Code Editor:
Select a code editor that suits your preferences. Popular choices include Visual Studio Code, Sublime Text, or JetBrains IDEs (like IntelliJ IDEA for Java).

Install a Version Control System (VCS):
Set up Git and configure it with your preferred VCS (e.g., GitHub, GitLab, or Bitbucket). This allows you to track changes and collaborate with others.

Set Up a Local Server Environment:
Install tools like XAMPP, WAMP, or Docker to create a local server environment for testing web applications.

Select a CSS Preprocessor:
If you’re working with CSS, consider using preprocessors like Sass or Less. Document the installation process and any customizations you make.

Choose a Front-End Framework:
If you’re building web applications, decide on a front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, or Vue.js). Include installation steps and any additional configurations.

